Z||000000||Little Duce Coupe||11-01-2001||12:53 PM||||I am interested in the form of racing where you and your co-pilot follow a specified route and clock your self trying to get as close to the time set by the race corridinators.<P>Two questions..<P>What is it called "officially"?<BR>&<BR>Does any group (or anybody) conduct these in for novice classes in California?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Little Duce Coupe<BR>"You Don't Know What She Costs"||||reg||5
Z||000001||TRiAD||11-01-2001||01:14 PM||||It's called "Road Rally", and try SCCA.org. <P>Good luck!<P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0NgAlAL0S2vLvViYU9P7uloj72fLFTqfz59trng8I7AOG7hGCvfk6WP96n!gnOaEUAvooy1kUoWucv7BJ7L5EWg/temp-sig.gif">    <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Archie||11-01-2001||08:05 PM||||It's called TSD Road Rally. TSD means Time Speed Distance.... I used to run them all the time.<P>You can find some thru the National SCCA web site. But don't stop looking there, many small local Sports Car Clubs (that have no affiliation with SCCA) put on TSD rallies.<P>When I used to run them I lived in Small town Indiana and one local club put on one Rally every month and another club put on 9 a year, so it was easy to find an event almost anytime you wanted one.<P>Archie<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Little Duce Coupe:<BR><B>I am interested in the form of racing where you and your co-pilot follow a specified route and clock your self trying to get as close to the time set by the race corridinators.<P>Two questions..<P>What is it called "officially"?<BR>&<BR>Does any group (or anybody) conduct these in for novice classes in California?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Little Duce Coupe||11-02-2001||03:45 PM||||Thanks!!<P>I've been interested and thought the Fiero would be a good/fun car for doing it in.<BR>(If you get in just the right position)<P>------------------<BR>Little Duce Coupe<BR>"You Don't Know What She Costs"||||reg||10
Z||000004||Borgio||11-02-2001||04:33 PM||||I've been to one of those type of races. They're awesome. I saw a fiero there, too. But it turns out it wasn't a fiero at all. It looked like a fiero, smelled sorta like a fiero, but it wasn't. After talking to the guy, I found out it was totally costum and that putting body panels on it put it in a different class. Pissed me off. It was a fastback and it was ruined. It was so low that they had to shave of part of the fenders and clip, by where the wheel wells were, or would be, who knows if this thing even had them. Why use a fastback?||||reg||1
